---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Vector Atlas - Outbreak Intelligence"
description: "A geographic atlas of disease vectors, ecological ranges, and transmission corridors."
active: vectors
permalink: /vector-atlas.html
pageCss: /assets/css/vector-atlas.css
pageJs: /assets/js/vector-atlas.js
headScripts:
  - "<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/d3@7/dist/d3.min.js\"></script>"
  - "<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/topojson-client@3/dist/topojson-client.min.js\"></script>"
---
<main class="atlas">
  <section class="atlas-hero">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Ecology of contagion</span>
      <h1 class="disp">Vector Atlas</h1>
      <p class="lede">A map of carriers and corridors: mosquitoes, fleas, bats, rodents, livestock, and human travel routes that turn local infections into regional histories.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="atlas-stats" aria-label="Atlas summary">
      <div><span class="n">6</span><span class="k">vector systems</span></div>
      <div><span class="n">19</span><span class="k">mapped signals</span></div>
      <div><span class="n">5</span><span class="k">eras</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="atlas-deck" aria-label="Interactive vector atlas">
    <aside class="atlas-controls">
      <div class="control-block">
        <span class="control-label">Vector layer</span>
        <div class="vector-buttons" id="vectorButtons"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="control-block">
        <span class="control-label">Historical lens</span>
        <div class="era-buttons" id="eraButtons"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="control-block selected-card" id="selectedCard">
        <span class="control-label">Selected system</span>
        <h2 class="disp">Mosquito Empire</h2>
        <p>Malaria, yellow fever, dengue, chikungunya, and Zika follow warm water, dense settlement, ports, and expanding urban edges.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="control-block atlas-legend">
        <span class="control-label">Reading the map</span>
        <ul class="legend-list">
          <li><span class="lg-mark lg-dot"></span>Field site — a known reservoir or outbreak locus</li>
          <li><span class="lg-mark lg-arc"></span>Corridor — a documented transmission route</li>
          <li><span class="lg-mark lg-swatch"></span>Colour — the active vector system</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="legend-note">Drag the globe to rotate. Era chips reveal how corridors accumulate over time. Click a site for detail.</p>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <div class="atlas-map-shell">
      <svg id="vectorGlobe" class="globe-svg" role="img" aria-label="Rotatable globe of disease-vector systems and transmission corridors"></svg>
      <div id="vectorFallback" class="vector-fallback" hidden>
        <span class="eyebrow">Vector field</span>
        <p>The globe could not load. Transmission corridors, reservoir zones, and carrier ranges remain described in the panel and notes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="map-caption">
        <span id="atlasStatus">Mosquito layer · surveillance lens</span>
        <span>Drag to rotate · click a site</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="atlas-notes">
    <article>
      <span class="eyebrow">Reading the map</span>
      <h2 class="disp">Vectors are not footnotes. They are infrastructure.</h2>
      <p>Every outbreak has a setting. Some settings are bodies of water, grain stores, slaughter corridors, migration routes, or clinics at the edge of a forest. The atlas treats vectors as a geographic system, not a single organism.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span class="eyebrow">Use</span>
      <h2 class="disp">Switch layers. Follow routes. Compare eras.</h2>
      <p>The page is built for editorial exploration: each layer changes map color, active range, field sites, and connecting routes. The era chips shift the frame from antiquity to modern surveillance.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</main>
